      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LUX AETERNA (8) is a talented mare who has been going well in Sydney, drawing out and racing three wide without cover but sticking on to go under by only 3m in her latest attempt at Listed level. Kept fresh since and draws on the back row but has won four of five tries at this distance. Class will carry her a long way. The ace draw should suit ISLA ROCHELLE (1) perfectly. She continued her consistent form when runner-up at Albion Park last time. She gets every chance to return to the winners' list. FARFALLA STRIDE (7) made a winning start in Queensland when overcoming a wide barrier at Albion Park last week. More depth here but she goes well at the distance and draws to trail ISLA ROCHELLE. She could be dangerous. TREMENDOUS SENSATION NZ (5) won over this distance the only time she raced here. Respect.",
